$\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ -2 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} \times \begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \\ z \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -2z + 2y \\ 2z - x \\ -x - y \end{pmatrix}.$
This gives $2(-x - y) = 0,$ $2z - x = 0,$ and $-2z + 2y = 0.$  Hence, $\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ -2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}.$
